        "section": "medicine",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "05 - Endocrine and Metabolic Drugs",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nRAPID-ACTING (meal coverage, onset 15 min, peak 1–2h, duration 3–5h):\n  Lispro (Humalog), aspart (NovoLog), glulisine (Apidra)\n  Analog: amino acid sequence modification → ↓ self-aggregation → faster absorption\n  Fast-acting inhaled (Afrezza): ultra-rapid (peak ~15 min); lung delivery; no injection\n  Fiasp (aspart + niacinamide): faster still; \"ultra-rapid\""
    },
    {
      "id": "05-ENDOCRINE-METABOLIC.md#010",
      "path": [
        "05-ENDOCRINE-METABOLIC.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:medicine:05-endocrine-metabolic, git-history:medicine:05-endocrine-metabolic]",
        "canonical_path": "medicine/05-ENDOCRINE-METABOLIC.md",
        "concepts": "[endocrine, metabolic]",
        "current_path": "medicine/05-ENDOCRINE-METABOLIC.md",
        "id": "maxim:medicine:endocrine-metabolic",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "medicine",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[endocrine, metabolic]",
        "section": "medicine",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "05 - Endocrine and Metabolic Drugs",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "SHORT-ACTING (Regular insulin, onset 30–60 min, peak 2–4h, duration 6–8h):\n  Regular (R) insulin: only insulin FDA-approved for IV infusion\n  IV use: DKA management, hyperkalemia treatment, perioperative insulin infusion\n  PO: must be given 30 min before meals (slower onset) → less convenient than rapid-acting"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-ENDOCRINE-METABOLIC.md#011",
      "path": [
        "05-ENDOCRINE-METABOLIC.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:medicine:05-endocrine-metabolic, git-history:medicine:05-endocrine-metabolic]",
        "canonical_path": "medicine/05-ENDOCRINE-METABOLIC.md",
        "concepts": "[endocrine, metabolic]",
        "current_path": "medicine/05-ENDOCRINE-METABOLIC.md",
        "id": "maxim:medicine:endocrine-metabolic",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "medicine",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[endocrine, metabolic]",
        "section": "medicine",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "05 - Endocrine and Metabolic Drugs",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "INTERMEDIATE-ACTING (NPH, onset 2–4h, peak 4–10h, duration 12–18h):\n  NPH (protamine + regular): cloudy suspension; twice daily\n  Significant peak → hypoglycemia risk; variable absorption\n  Largely replaced by long-acting analogs but still used in some protocols"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-ENDOCRINE-METABOLIC.md#012",
      "path": [
        "05-ENDOCRINE-METABOLIC.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:medicine:05-endocrine-metabolic, git-history:medicine:05-endocrine-metabolic]",
        "canonical_path": "medicine/05-ENDOCRINE-METABOLIC.md",
        "concepts": "[endocrine, metabolic]",
        "current_path": "medicine/05-ENDOCRINE-METABOLIC.md",
        "id": "maxim:medicine:endocrine-metabolic",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "medicine",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[endocrine, metabolic]",
        "section": "medicine",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "05 - Endocrine and Metabolic Drugs",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "LONG-ACTING (basal insulin, onset 1–2h, nearly peakless, duration 18–24h or longer):\n  Glargine (Lantus/Basaglar/Toujeo): precipitates at SC injection pH → slow absorption\n    Toujeo (U-300): 3× concentrated → longer duration (~36h); less nocturnal hypoglycemia\n  Detemir (Levemir): albumin-binding → extended action; twice daily (shorter t½ than glargine)\n  Degludec (Tresiba): forms multi-hexamers → very long t½ (25h) → 42h duration → dosing flexibility"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-ENDOCRINE-METABOLIC.md#013",
      "path": [
        "05-ENDOCRINE-METABOLIC.md"
      ],
